{"agent":"bg41","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_only_ids` returns `True` for any title where every `\\w+` token merely contains at least one digit — it never compares the title to the item’s actual id or an id grammar. For example, an item with title `\"l10n\"` (a real localization title) or `\"iPhone15\"` has no non-digit word, so `_only_ids` returns `True`. `_untitled` then reports that item as having “no title of their own, only the id,” which is false and turns the doctor note into a false positive for meaningful alphanumeric titles.","digest":"e14e42ed6c42ca46","location":"ddflow/api/reporting/health_notes.py:_only_ids","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/reporting/health_notes.py:_only_ids"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"The test no longer exercises the MCP `ddflow_complete` path it is named after and that the bug report lists. It now calls `run_cli(repo, \"complete\", \"T1\", \"--force\", \"--model\", \"x\")` and asserts CLI stdout rather than calling `_call(repo, \"ddflow_complete\", ...)` and checking `body[\"progress\"]`. A future change that makes MCP `ddflow_complete` return `{\"ok\": True}` without a `progress` field on successful forced completion will still leave this test green, so the MCP regression is no longer covered.","digest":"f6118d64fbb0c843","location":"tests/test_progress_line_mcp.py:31-32 (test_mcp_complete_carries_the_progress_block)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_progress_line_mcp.py:31-32 (test_mcp_complete_carries_the_progress_block)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_mcp_complete_carries_the_progress_block` no longer calls MCP. It runs CLI `complete T1 --force --model x` and only checks that stdout contains `Progress: tasks 1/1 (100%)`. An MCP `ddflow_complete` result that omits the `progress` key (the contract the old assertion `body[\"progress\"].startswith(\"Progress: tasks 1/1 (100%)\")` enforced) still passes. Sharing `finish.complete` does not cover MCP serialization of that block, so the named regression is gone.","digest":"c3b4715ead96a09e","location":"tests/test_progress_line_mcp.py:32","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_progress_line_mcp.py:32"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21785,"diff_sha":"bc96da035f447f98a60d1949c653785f68a4d68af47296f98885d84e64a64053","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.9,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"c52ed3654ab97b8a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B328649c6ed.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T195455Z-09532290.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"9887cdbc4d866b6e459ea7ee8b75f5daeeafcc58","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/reporting/health.py":"100644 c1f49bcbe7787e266edae9b6168efe0f76c4d594","ddflow/api/reporting/health_notes.py":"100644 ab1e268fede6b1eaf51836429d56e528d45861af","ddflow/api/reporting/vigil.py":"100644 12ebce0411294ad498cdd0f9503d62bb79170337","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.api.reporting.health.toml":"","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.api.reporting.health_notes.toml":"100644 ef2a92d403598afce1adf785685ffd8ed39b70aa","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.fleet.toml":"","tests/test_command_registry.py":"100644 5b52ae584af591d44201e3b53ec69a5d0eb8ec93","tests/test_no_agent_literals.py":"100644 e0cb9af2838d630858a59fda8f996f4d83ff3e8f","tests/test_progress_line_mcp.py":"100644 d8b587ba68848b3ae37668874da98e3bd59340c8","tests/test_remedy_texts.py":"100644 1b3153e4ab71bbf5ac58939209e85882eccee717"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/reporting/health_notes.py:_only_ids","tests/